Package: com.iosvcam.opencam
Name: iOS-VCAM OpenCam
Version: 0.5.2
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Open-source, editable virtual camera tweak. Runs in mediaserverd so it covers every capture client (stock Camera, TikTok, all apps). Pulls an RTMP stream on-device, decodes H264 via VideoToolbox, and overwrites the camera's OWN image buffer IN PLACE at BWNodeOutput -emitSampleBuffer: with a SINGLE GPU-accelerated VTPixelTransferSessionTransferImage (one pass, no per-frame pixel rotation, no CVPixelBuffer lock around the transfer), then passes the ORIGINAL sample buffer downstream - matching the closed vcamera's GPU sync discipline (render nodes stay pass-through; orientation is carried by the pipeline's existing metadata). Every client reads the same overwritten upstream IOSurface, so the app preview shows OBS. Fail-open everywhere (any error falls back to the real camera). NOTE: the global microphone/audio hook (VCamAudioMS.x) is temporarily out of this build while the video path is verified; it returns in a later version. 0.5.2: ellekit-safe install/removal on RootHide - the /usr/lib/TweakInject mirror no longer clobbers or orphans RootHide AutoPatcher's own copy, so removing the package no longer breaks ellekit.
Maintainer: iOS-VCAM
Author: iOS-VCAM
Section: Tweaks
Depends: mobilesubstrate (>= 0.9.5000)
Conflicts: com.x.vcamera, com.iosvcam.audiobridge, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.system-hook, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-active, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-probe, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.daemon, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.safe
Replaces: com.x.vcamera, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-active, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.safe
